## Voxels, 6: an endless world. Walk in any direction and it never ends:
## the land comes from value noise hashed from the coordinates
## (vx:h_eightsAt), so any column of 16 by 16 blocks can be made by
## itself and fits its neighbors; columns are made around the player as
## it walks -- the nearest missing one each frame -- and dropped behind
## it; fog hides the edge of what is made, and a curved horizon (scene
## lowers the world by d^2 / 2R) makes it look like a small planet.
## Collision asks the columns themselves. The world and the player are
## the library Endless.xtl, shared with voxels-fly: each column is made
## over three frames, so no frame waits long.
## Run: just demo scene voxels-endless
##   W A S D walk, Shift run, Space jump (in water: swim up; at the
##   surface: climb out onto a bank one block high), drag the mouse or
##   the arrows to look, H: back to the start, q or close: quit

"en:" u_se< "Endless"
"sc:" u_se< "Scene"

w := "Voxels 6: endless -- X_eTaL" sc:o_pen! 640 400
g := w sc:f_og! 22.0 44.0
k := w sc:s_ky! 0.55 0.72 0.92
k := w sc:c_urve! 160.0

"keys: W A S D walk, Shift run, Space jump (in water: swim up, climb out), drag or arrows look, H home, q quit"

## the world around the start made before the first frame: each column
## takes three steps
s := en:n_ew w
s := (3 * (1 + 2 * en:reach) * 1 + 2 * en:reach) 'en:s_tream p_ower s
"columns made at the start:"
t_ally en:k_eys s

## one frame: an event, then a third of a column's work, then the
## player
u:f_rame := { s ->
  en:s_topped s ? s
  v := sc:n_ext! w
  ((v m_atch "close") + (v m_atch "key q") + v m_atch "key Escape") > 0 ? en:s_top s
  s := (v m_atch "key h") u:i_f s
  s := en:s_tream s
  s en:m_ove sc:c_ontrols w
}
u:i_f := { yes s ->
  yes ? en:h_omeAgain s
  s
}
last := 100000 'u:f_rame p_ower s
z := sc:c_lose! w
"where the walk ended (x y z, blocks), the columns kept:"
(f_loat f_loor 0.5 + 3 t_ake en:p_layer last) c_at f_loat t_ally en:k_eys last
"bye"
